{{!--
    Renders a table from structured data for AsciiDoc.

    Parameters:
        headers: array of header cell strings (e.g. (arr "Name" "Description")).
                 Optional; if absent, no header row is emitted.
        items:   array of source items; one item per row.
        columns: array of dotted paths into each item; one path per
                 column. Use "." to mean "the item itself". Each extracted
                 value is dispatched through markup/cell, which routes by
                 `$meta.type` to the appropriate print partial. This partial
                 only reads fields; a caller that needs a referenced symbol
                 resolves the id to a symbol before passing `items` (see the
                 example), so every column here stays a plain field path.
        weights: optional array of relative column weights, e.g.
                 (arr 1 4) for a 1:4 ratio.  Format-agnostic data;
                 each format renders it as appropriate (AsciiDoc
                 emits `[cols="1,4"]`; HTML lets CSS handle widths).

    Example (the caller assembles each row with zip_objects: the "self"
    column keeps the reference for the name cell, while the "brief" column
    resolves the referenced symbol for the description cell):
        {{> markup/table
            weights=(arr 1 4)
            headers=(arr "Name" "Description")
            items=(zip_objects (arr "self" "brief")
                     symbol.friends
                     (pluck (transform (pluck symbol.friends "id") @root.mrdocs.corpus.get) "doc.brief"))
            columns=(arr "self" "brief") }}

    A trailing blank line follows so the next block parses cleanly.

    See: https://mrdocs.com/docs/mrdocs/develop/generators.html#dom_reference
--}}
[cols="{{#if weights}}{{#each weights}}{{#unless @first}},{{/unless}}{{this}}{{/each}}{{else}}{{#each columns}}{{#unless @first}},{{/unless}}1{{/each}}{{/if}}"]
|===
{{#if headers}}{{#each headers}}| {{this}}{{/each}}
{{/if~}}
{{#each items as | item |}}
{{#each ../columns as | column_spec |~}}
| {{> markup/cell (lookup item column_spec)}}
{{/each~}}
{{/each~}}
|===

